The Wayland stack of stage 11 lives in the tree (PLAN.md, "Этап 11";
PORTING-LOG.md, "Стек Wayland в дереве").  This directory keeps what is
not part of the system: the import script and the stands.

Where things are:

  external/mit/<pkg>/dist    the sources, as imported by import-stack.sh
  external/mit/<pkg>/...     reachover Makefiles (bsd.lib.mk, bsd.prog.mk),
                             config headers and generated files beside them
  external/bsd/evdev/dist    FreeBSD's input-event-codes.h (BSD-2)
  tools/wayland-scanner      nbwayland-scanner, the host's protocol compiler
                             (TOOL_WAYLAND_SCANNER)
  minix/lib/libgfxcompat     what the stack needs of the system that the
                             system has not got: <pthread.h> and <threads.h>
                             over libmthread, sem_*, <uchar.h> (UTF-8 always)
                             - headers in /usr/include/gfxcompat
  minix/usr.bin/meechowm     the compositor (tinywl with MEECHO's screen and
                             input, and windows as columns on a strip -
                             the keys are in meechowm.c)
  minix/tests/gfx            wlhello, the smallest client, /usr/tests/gfx

Packages: libffi 3.8.0, wayland 1.26.0, wayland-protocols 1.49, pixman
0.46.4 and libdrm 2.4.134 (NetBSD-current's xsrc dists), libxkbcommon
1.13.2, xkeyboard-config 2.38 (NetBSD's), wlroots 0.20.2, FreeType 2.15.0,
fontconfig 2.18.3, tllist 1.1.0, fcft 3.3.3, foot 1.28.0; expat is the
tree's (external/mit/expat).  Licences MIT or BSD-like, FreeType under its
FTL; nothing GPL is imported (import-stack.sh says what is left out).

Building, in this order (the first line once per tools build):

  nbmake-evbarm64-el -C tools/wayland-scanner obj dependall install
  port/build-dirs.sh minix/lib/libgfxcompat minix/lib/libepoll-shim \
      external/mit/expat external/mit/libffi external/mit/wayland \
      external/mit/wayland-protocols external/mit/pixman external/mit/libdrm \
      external/mit/libxkbcommon external/mit/xkeyboard-config \
      external/mit/wlroots external/mit/freetype external/mit/fontconfig \
      external/mit/tllist external/mit/fcft external/mit/foot \
      minix/usr.bin/meechowm minix/tests/gfx

New directories under /usr/include, /usr/share and /etc go into
etc/mtree/NetBSD.dist.base, and DESTDIR gets them from
"nbmake-evbarm64-el do-distrib-dirs".

  import-stack.sh    every dist from its source (~/gfx-src: shallow clones
                     of the upstream tags; ~/gfxport/nb-xsrc: NetBSD's xsrc)

  test/qemu-gfx.py   meechowm with no screen (headless) and wlhello, QEMU
  test/qemu-meechowm.py
                     meechowm on QEMU's fb (virtual=1), the screen read back
                     through /dev/fb0: window, cursor, foot, console back
  test/board-meechowm.sh
                     the same on the board, over ssh, left running for
                     whoever is at the monitor
  test/board-cursorload.sh
                     what moving the cursor costs on the board
  test/board-scroll.sh
                     4.4 MB scrolled through foot on the board: time,
                     kern.cp_time and the md5 of the frame it ends on
                     (the same with PIXMAN_DISABLE=arm-neon and without)
  test/striptest.sh  the strip's arithmetic (meechowm's layout.c) on the
                     host: widths, the view, random walks
  test/qemu-strip.py the strip on QEMU's fb: three windows, the keys
                     (usb_kbd inject= chords), motion caught half way, a
                     click, panels (wlhello -L, yambar), a terminal, the
                     palette (fuzzel) - each step against meechowm -m state
                     and the screen
  test/qemu-shot.py  a picture of the desktop as a PNG: panel, foot, a
                     window, with -p the palette open; the frame comes
                     from /dev/fb0 through gzip and uuencode on the console
  test/qemu-mode.py  the screen's mode changed under a running desktop
                     (meechowm -m mode), against state and pixels, the
                     console taking the new size after it, fbmode(8)
                     changing it from the console, and monitors plugged
                     in (the virtual display's: ../test/fb/fbvplug.c)
  test/board-shot.sh the board's screen as a PNG, over ssh from Git Bash:
                     fbart says the geometry, dd reads /dev/fb0, fbpng.py
                     (in WSL) writes it
  test/fcftprobe.c   what foot asks of fcft, alone, with fcft's debug log
  test/uchartest.sh  libgfxcompat's uchar.c against glibc in C.UTF-8, on
                     the host
  ../test/fb/fbart.c the screen (or an area of it) as text, from /dev/fb0

The stands take the font from the host (DejaVu Sans Mono, Bitstream Vera
licence); it is not in the tree.

Until 2026-10-13 this directory held the prototype: every package built by
its own meson or autotools against a copy of DESTDIR (build-stack.sh,
cc.sh, cross-meecho.ini), its changes in patches/, the compat code in
compat/ - in git history from c507a9bbe to the commit that moved it.
